<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n102761" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τεγέα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ας</span>, 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τεγέη</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ης</span>, ἡ, <u>Tegea</u> in
		Arcadia, <i><span class="en">
			Il.
			2.607
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>O.</u>
			10(11).66
		</span></i>, etc.:—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τεγεάτης</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span></span>, 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τᾰχῠ-ήτης</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or
				<i>from Tegea</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.65
			</span></i>, etc.; then, by a play upon words, <i>of</i> or <i>from a
				brothel</i> (v. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					111
				</span></i>
			), Diog.Cyn. ap. <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				6.61
			</span></i>: fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τεγεᾶτις</span></b> ,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>, (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χώρα</span>) <i>the Tegeate country</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				5.65
			</span></i>:—Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τεγεᾱτικός</span></b> , 
				Ion.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τᾰχῠ-ητικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.124
			</span></i>.</div>
